<%#
  The confirmation a reporter gets. It echoes NOTHING they typed — not the subject, not the
  message. The form is open to anybody and sends to whatever address is typed into it, so a
  confirmation that repeated the text would let a stranger put their own words in an email
  from us to somebody who never asked. The reference and fixed sentences only.
-%>
<p>Thank you — your <%= isIdea ? 'idea' : 'report' %> reached <%= appName %>.</p>
<p style="font-size:18px;margin:16px 0"><strong>Your reference: <%= reference %></strong></p>
<p>A person reads every <%= isIdea ? 'idea' : 'report' %>, and the reply comes to this address. Quote the reference if you write to us about it.</p>
<% if (mineUrl) { %>
  <p style="margin:24px 0">
    <a href="<%= mineUrl %>"
       style="background:#0b5cab;color:#ffffff;padding:12px 22px;border-radius:8px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;display:inline-block">
      See its status
    </a>
  </p>
<% } %>
<p style="font-size:13px;color:#6b7280">
  If you did not send this, you can ignore this email — nothing else will be sent to you about it.
</p>
